  "notes": [
    "5 V logic: outputs swing to 5 V, which is too much for 3.3 V parts (ESP32, Pico, BME280 bare). Inputs read HIGH above 3.0 V (0.6 x VCC), so a 3.3 V signal is read correctly but with little margin.",
    "Per-pin current: 20 mA recommended, 40 mA absolute max, 200 mA total for the chip. Never drive a motor or servo directly from a pin.",
    "Power: USB (5 V, limited to 500 mA by a polyfuse), or 7-12 V on VIN / the barrel jack (6-20 V absolute). Feeding 5 V into the 5V pin bypasses the regulator and its protection; only do it from a clean regulated 5 V supply and never together with VIN.",
    "A4/A5 are the I2C pins, repeated as SDA/SCL next to AREF on R3 boards. The Wire library enables weak (20-50 kOhm) internal pull-ups to 5 V.",
    "D0/D1 are shared with USB serial; D13 has the onboard LED.",
    "PWM pins: 3, 5, 6, 9, 10, 11 (marked with ~ on the board)."
  ],
